{"name": "Ram Jhula", "slug": "ram-jhula", "type": "cultural", "curatedDistrict": "Dehradun", "region": "Garhwal", "location": "Rishikesh, across the Ganges", "category": "", "highlightCandidates": ["suspension bridge", "Sivananda", "Ganga", "Geeta Bhawan"], "articleTitle": "Ram Jhula", "site": "wikipedia", "wikidataQid": "Q7288488", "coords": {"lat": 30.123238, "lon": 78.314438}, "onPageImages": ["File:Akashi-kaikyo bridge3.jpg", "File:India Uttaranchal locator map.svg", "File:Ramjhula - bridge over the Ganga.jpg"], "pageimage": "Ramjhula_-_bridge_over_the_Ganga.jpg", "pageUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ram_Jhula", "extract": "Ram Jhula  (Hindi: राम झूला) is an iron suspension bridge across the river Ganges, located 3 kilometres (1.9 mi) north-east from the center of the city of  Rishikesh in the Indian state of Uttarakhand. The bridge connects the Sivananda Nagar area of Muni Ki Reti in the Tehri Garhwal district to the Swargashram area of Rishikesh in the Pauri Garhwal district, crossing the river from west to east. Built in the year 1986, the bridge is one of the iconic landmarks of Rishikesh.\nThere are many Hindu ashrams and religious centers established on both sides of the Ganges. Ram Jhula is also a connecting bridge between Sivananda Ashram located in Muni Ki Reti to Gita Bhawan, Parmarth Niketan and other temples located in Swargashram. Though similar in design, this bridge is bigger than Lakshman Jhula, which is 2 kilometres (1.2 mi) up the river. This bridge is constructed with a span of 750 feet (230 m).\nMotorbikes and two wheelers had been restricted from crossing on the bridge and only pedestrian access remained allowed as of 2023 as reported by The Hindu. As of 2025, the bridge is completely closed as reported by Dainik Jagran newspaper.\n\n\nReferences", "wikivoyageExtract": null, "coverImage": {"url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_11.jpg/1920px-Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_11.jpg", "source": "Wikimedia Commons", "sourcePage": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_11.jpg", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0)", "attribution": "Goutam1962 — Own work", "alt": "Devotees and Tourist Enjoying the Sunset at Rishikesh Ram jhula"}, "coverImageLowerResolution": false, "gallery": [{"url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_14.jpg/1920px-Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_14.jpg", "source": "Wikimedia Commons", "sourcePage": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_14.jpg", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0)", "attribution": "Goutam1962 — Own work", "alt": "Devotees and Tourist Enjoying the Sunset at Rishikesh Ram jhula"}, {"url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_09.jpg/1920px-Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_09.jpg", "source": "Wikimedia Commons", "sourcePage": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_09.jpg", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0)", "attribution": "Goutam1962 — Own work", "alt": "Devotees and Tourist Enjoying the Sunset at Rishikesh Ram jhula"}, {"url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_12.jpg/1920px-Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_12.jpg", "source": "Wikimedia Commons", "sourcePage": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devotees_and_Tourist_Enjoying_the_Sunset_at_Rishikesh_Ram_jhula_12.jpg", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0